{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01331",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.09,
      "end_seconds": 6.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Doctor? Hello, I hope this is the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.31,
      "end_seconds": 11.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.83,
      "end_seconds": 28.98,
      "duration_seconds": 16.15,
      "text": "I wanted to get skipped beats looked at i didn't want to make a fuss, you know i'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.43,
      "end_seconds": 33.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.27,
      "end_seconds": 39.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "I've, I've had it since this morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.95,
      "end_seconds": 49.19,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "I follow tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.51,
      "end_seconds": 59.07,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "Mm, yes, caffeine. That makes it worse. I'd say a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.09,
      "end_seconds": 63.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.4,
      "end_seconds": 75.1,
      "duration_seconds": 10.7,
      "text": "It, It usually comes with being a bit anxious. About being a bit anxious, pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.09,
      "end_seconds": 80.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Right, have you noticed shortness of breath, dizziness or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.35,
      "end_seconds": 83.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "nope, nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.46,
      "end_seconds": 87.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "What about chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.94,
      "end_seconds": 92.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.2,
      "end_seconds": 97.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "how are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.0,
      "end_seconds": 101.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.5,
      "end_seconds": 106.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Alright, has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.66,
      "end_seconds": 110.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "ah, nothing on the skin, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.89,
      "end_seconds": 114.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.12,
      "end_seconds": 127.36,
      "duration_seconds": 11.24,
      "text": "I, I had an operation for a hernia last spring. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.79,
      "end_seconds": 132.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "let's talk a little about your daily life and habits"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.46,
      "end_seconds": 146.39,
      "duration_seconds": 12.93,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.86,
      "end_seconds": 151.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.13,
      "end_seconds": 155.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "It's simvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.08,
      "end_seconds": 159.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.05,
      "end_seconds": 166.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "for six months. Herbal calming tea i take it in the evening"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.19,
      "end_seconds": 170.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.09,
      "end_seconds": 174.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "About about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.48,
      "end_seconds": 192.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions. These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.86,
      "end_seconds": 196.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "High cholesterol, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.84,
      "end_seconds": 202.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.06,
      "end_seconds": 205.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.71,
      "end_seconds": 211.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.29,
      "end_seconds": 218.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Let me think, my father had bowel cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.04,
      "end_seconds": 232.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.69,
      "end_seconds": 247.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Okay, that's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.99,
      "end_seconds": 277.04,
      "duration_seconds": 11.05,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.7 degrees, SpO2 98 percent on room air. And blood pressure 110 over 81, pulse is 74 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.82,
      "end_seconds": 279.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.41,
      "end_seconds": 284.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.72,
      "end_seconds": 291.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.15,
      "end_seconds": 295.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.96,
      "end_seconds": 308.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "your pulse is regular and your heart sounds are normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.79,
      "end_seconds": 310.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.73,
      "end_seconds": 325.19,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. So where does that leave us? It points towards harmless extra heartbeats."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.64,
      "end_seconds": 330.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "I mean, do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.96,
      "end_seconds": 349.56,
      "duration_seconds": 17.6,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like harmless extra heartbeats, but I'd like to confirm. Just to be sure I understood. You've had skipped beats, since this morning, and no shortness of breath or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.62,
      "end_seconds": 351.32,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.17,
      "end_seconds": 383.71,
      "duration_seconds": 13.54,
      "text": "I want an ECG done, that's for palpitations. If you faint or have chest pain, that's the point to come in urgently. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.97,
      "end_seconds": 389.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.8,
      "end_seconds": 392.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}